      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): serialize tool call arguments as JSON strings for Ollama…",
        "body": "What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where users chatting with an Ollama Cloud model (kimi-k2.5:cloud, glm-5.2:cloud, etc.) would get a failed response on the second message whenever the first turn used a tool call. Local Ollama was unaffected.\r\n\r\nWhy This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nWhen replaying the conversation history for a second turn, extractToolCalls built the assistant message with arguments as a JS object. After JSON.stringify on the full request body, that object serialized as an inline JSON value — but Ollama Cloud enforces the OpenAI spec which requires arguments to be a pre-encoded JSON string. Stringifying inside extractToolCalls fixes both paths: local Ollama already types arguments as Record<string,unknown>|string so it accepts the string form, and cloud Ollama now gets what it expects.\r\n\r\nUser Impact\r\n\r\nOllama Cloud models now complete multi-turn conversations that include tool calls. Previously every turn after the first would fail when any tool was used.\r\n\r\nEvidence\r\n\r\nExisting test suite updated: 9 assertions in stream-runtime.test.ts that previously documented the object form now assert the string form, confirming the correct wire format for both toolCall and tool_use block types. The \"preserves unsafe integers\" test also passes correctly since parseJsonObjectPreservingUnsafeIntegers converts large integers to strings before re-serialization.\r\n<img width=\"1037\" height=\"242\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-08 at 10 22 47 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f0c491a-b573-41d5-912b-e5af8d49c4da\" />\r\n<img width=\"1037\" height=\"242\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-08 at 10 23 04 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/298f07fb-bd4b-42da-a28d-c51473629fb2\" />\r\n\r\nCloses #102200.",
